{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1529468690,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzM5MTk2NTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2667","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad.testing to provide helpers for developers to use DataLad","message":"It came up in the context of heudiconv tests which already use DataLad to download a sample dataset for testing.  The problem is that we do not have any type of fixture to share the same dataset across multiple runs of tests so it downloads it over and over again.  Instead of coming up with a (pytest) fixture we (with @leej3) thought it would be nice if datalad provided `.testing` module (similar to the one in numpy and other toolkits like pymvpa) which either provided testing platform specific fixtures or just helper functions like `get_testing_dataset(\"///openfmri/ds0000001\", version=\"1.0.0-or-hexsha\", get='sub*')`","files":null}]}